  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37131332",
      "title": "Understanding \"if\" Statements",
      "lectureOrder": 64,
      "videoOrder": 60,
      "sourceHash": "0dffbd379b538c7bfa18593d9a67e8e955d10e2ac3bc63c513a3ab09a7f98f86",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.785,
          "end": 4.59,
          "en": "So, you can use ternary expressions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.59,
          "end": 6.72,
          "en": "in your widget tree, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.72,
          "end": 10.186,
          "en": "to dynamically derive a value based on some condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.186,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "or based on some other value in the end, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 17.07,
          "en": "In this case, based on the value stored in activeScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.07,
          "end": 20.55,
          "en": "But adding such ternary expressions here in the widget tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.55,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "can also make the code a bit harder to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "It also might be easy to overlook this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 28.29,
          "en": "and therefore, you might prefer an alternative approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.29,
          "end": 30.45,
          "en": "which I also wanna show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.45,
          "end": 33.72,
          "en": "Instead of using this ternary expression down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 36.12,
          "en": "you could also go to your build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.12,
          "end": 37.17,
          "en": "which is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.17,
          "end": 39.553,
          "en": "when the widget is rendered for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.553,
          "end": 42.3,
          "en": "and after set state is called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "And in there, you could introduce a new variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 48.87,
          "en": "which is now only available inside of the build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 51.36,
          "en": "So, this is now not a class variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.36,
          "end": 53.16,
          "en": "it's not like activeScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.16,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "which is available in the entire class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 58.68,
          "en": "but instead, it's a variable scoped to this build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "and only available in this build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.89,
          "en": "And this variable could have a name of screenWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.89,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "though the name, as always, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.946,
          "en": "And it could initially be set to StartScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.946,
          "end": 75.243,
          "en": "which still receives the switchScreen function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "But now, I wanna make sure that screenWidget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 80.52,
          "en": "is set to a different value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.52,
          "end": 85.05,
          "en": "if activeScreen is not start-screen, but questions-screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 88.752,
          "en": "To achieve this, we could cut this ternary expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.752,
          "end": 90.57300000000001,
          "en": "and use that up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.92,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "And then we could actually even set this to final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "because now this never changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 99.281,
          "en": "It's only set once whenever the build method runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.281,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "either to StartScreen or to QuestionsScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 104.40899999999999,
          "en": "and you could then use screenWidget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.40899999999999,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "as a value down there for child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "so that the value stored in screenWidget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "is passed as a value to the child argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 115.074,
          "en": "and that screen widget value is derived dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.074,
          "end": 117.90299999999999,
          "en": "with a ternary expression up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "You could do that, but with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.24,
          "en": "you would, of course, still be using a ternary expression,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.24,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "though, now at least outside of the widget tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 129.78,
          "en": "which already could be considered to be a bit more readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.78,
          "end": 131.88,
          "en": "But I want to show you a different approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.88,
          "end": 134.485,
          "en": "Hence, I'll go back to storing StartScreen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.485,
          "end": 138.03,
          "en": "as an initial value in screenWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.03,
          "end": 140.4,
          "en": "and I'll set this back to be a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.4,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "because now I conditionally want to set screenWidget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 148.46,
          "en": "to QuestionsScreen if a certain condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.458,
          "end": 151.32,
          "en": "Now, for that, first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.32,
          "end": 153.42000000000002,
          "en": "the type here for a screenWidget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 155.64,
          "en": "should explicitly be set to Widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.64,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "so that it's not inferred in a too-restrictive way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "We did that a couple of lectures ago already, if you recall.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "But now this code here should be executed conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "and for that, you can use another keyword provided by Dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 171.337,
          "en": "the if keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.337,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "That's a crucial keyword, which you need to use a lot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 176.7,
          "en": "which is why I'm introducing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.7,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "because if allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "to specify a condition between parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 185.19,
          "en": "and then you add opening and closing curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "and the code between these curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 190.8,
          "en": "will then only be executed if this condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.8,
          "end": 192.54,
          "en": "So, now we could cut this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 196.707,
          "en": "and paste this here into this if statement body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.707,
          "end": 199.23,
          "en": "and the condition that should be specified here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.23,
          "end": 203.7,
          "en": "is now almost the same as before in the ternary expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.7,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "We wanna compare activeScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 207,
          "en": "So, this variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207,
          "end": 210.24,
          "en": "which is dynamically updated if the button was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.24,
          "end": 212.61,
          "en": "We wanna check if it's equal to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 212.61,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "questions-screen now actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "because we then set screenWidget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 220.828,
          "en": "to QuestionsScreen if the identifier is equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 220.828,
          "end": 222.903,
          "en": "to questions-screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 226.56,
          "en": "And here, we can add const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 226.56,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "And with that, whenever the build method executes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 232.90699999999998,
          "en": "the screenWidget variable is initially set to StartScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 232.90699999999998,
          "end": 235.41,
          "en": "but it then might be overwritten",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 235.41,
          "end": 237.93,
          "en": "if this condition is met here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 237.93,
          "end": 240.51,
          "en": "So, if activeScreen is questions-screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 240.51,
          "end": 242.91,
          "en": "then screenWidget would be overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 242.91,
          "end": 244.41,
          "en": "And that's an alternative pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 244.41,
          "end": 246.78,
          "en": "of setting content conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 248.55,
          "en": "because now screenWidget can of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 248.55,
          "end": 250.98,
          "en": "be used down there as a value for a child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 253.29,
          "en": "and therefore, will now either be StartScreen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 257.193,
          "en": "or a QuestionsScreen that is set as a value for child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 258.21,
          "end": 261.18,
          "en": "And that's the last alternative I wanted to show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 261.18,
          "end": 263.64,
          "en": "If we save this and force a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 263.64,
          "end": 265.71,
          "en": "the app still works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 265.71,
          "end": 267.39,
          "en": "but now using this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 267.39,
          "end": 268.86,
          "en": "And as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.86,
          "end": 271.26,
          "en": "I simply showed all these different approaches,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 271.26,
          "end": 273.65999999999997,
          "en": "because we'll need them from time to time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.65999999999997,
          "end": 274.493,
          "en": "throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 274.493,
          "end": 276.33,
          "en": "And as a Flutter and Dart developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 276.33,
          "end": 279.45,
          "en": "you, of course, must know about these different approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 279.45,
          "end": 281.85,
          "en": "so that you can solve the different problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 281.85,
          "end": 284.88,
          "en": "you might be facing when working on your own project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 284.88,
          "end": 287.97,
          "en": "or also when working together with other colleagues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 290.58299999999997,
          "en": "that might be using one of these approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
